{"availability":"available","full":"STP-KAS/kaspa-master-file","name":"kaspa-master-file","description":"Experimental. Not advice.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-05T21:32:38Z","updated":"2026-10-08T16:52:41Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://demo.kaspa-x402.org/health","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T20:07:38.802Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T20:07:38.802Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T20:07:38.802Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:17:21.903Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-06T16:29:30.200Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T20:07:38.802Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Kaspa is a proof-of-work cryptocurrency: miners secure it by spending computing power. It had a fair launch in November 2021, with no premine, so no coins were set aside before public mining began. Instead of a single chain of blocks it keeps a blockDAG: blocks found at the same time all stay in the record, and a rule called GHOSTDAG puts them in order. The Crescendo upgrade brought mainnet to about 10 blocks a second. The Toccata upgrade turned on covenants on the base layer (L1) at DAA score 474165565. A covenant is a rule that a coin carries about how it may be spent next. The DAA score is…","This file is a public pin list for Kaspa and the work around it: the node software, the KIPs (Kaspa Improvement Proposals), covenant conventions, research code, workshop threads, and proposals that are still open. Each claim names the commit or the file it rests on, so anyone can open it and check.","Third-party builders and community projects live in STP-KAS/kaspa-builders."],"features":["A merged KIP with the status Active is the rule.","An open pull request is a proposal until it is merged.","DAGKnight (KIP-2, a consensus proposal) is still a proposal.","About 100 blocks a second is a later target, not som